meta {
  name: 4 Update customer
  type: http
  seq: 4
}
put {
  url: {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/customers/{{customerEmail}}
  body: json
}
body:json {
  {
    "firstName": "Ada",
    "lastName": "Lovelace-Updated",
    "email": "{{customerEmail}}"
  }
}
docs {
  **This is the route that proves the central 403 works.** F-016 deliberately **removed** its local
  `try/catch (ForbiddenException)` so nothing but `AgendaBuddyExceptionHandler` turns the guard's
  exception into a `403`. Before F-016 this line without a catch produced a `500` — and in `Production`,
  a bare empty-bodied one.

  Log in as one user and change `{{customerEmail}}` to another to see it: `403` with
  `{type, title, status, traceId, requestId}` and **no exception type, message or stack frame** in any
  environment (threat T-004).
}
